[[File:S1E24 Huntik council painting.png|thumb|200px|A 1900s painting showing the meeting of the first [[Huntik Foundation Council|Huntik Council]]]]
The Huntik Foundation was created early in the 20th century by a group of like minded [[Seekers]] who wanted to learn the secrets of the Titans. {{Source|Huntik.com}} The first [[Huntik Foundation Council]] was established at some point after 1959, to deliberate plans and missions. It consisted of seven members, including [[Eathon Lambert]]. A painting of the first meeting was hung on the wall of the [[Huntik Foundation Italian HQ|Huntik Italian HQ]]. {{source|The Secret of Two Generations}} The Huntik Council eventually became based at [[Huntik International HQ]] in [[Manhattan, New York]], while maintaining additional operational bases throughout the world. {{Source|Coming of Age}}

When [[the Organization]] revealed itself in 1959, the Foundation recognised the threat it posed to the world. They strove to uncover the lost Titans before they could be discovered and used for evil by [[the Professor]] and his followers. {{Source|The Secret of Two Generations}}

At some point, the Foundation was successfully infiltrated by the Organization, with information on the [[Prague Huntik Hotel]] somehow being passed onto [[DeFoe]]'s [[Suits]]. {{Source|Words of Truth, Heart of Lies}} The double agent was revealed to be [[Zhalia Moon]], who had been raised by the Organization scientist, [[Klaus]]. {{Source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}} However, Zhalia repented for her betrayal and was made an official member by [[Metz]] after helping the Foundation obtain the [[Ring]] of [[Behemoth]], the [[Legendary Titan]] of Body. {{Source|Ladies' Choice}}

The Foundation were shocked by the revelation that the Professor was, in fact, Simon Judeau, and had once been a member of the Huntik Foundation. {{Source|The Secret of Two Generations}} The Foundation were officially against Dante Vale's team travelling to [[the Professor's castle]] due to the danger and recklessness of the mission, but did not stand in their way. {{Source|The Divine Comedy}} The Huntik team, in turn, succeeded in defeating the Professor for good. {{Source|The Mission}} Despite this, the threat of the Organization continued to trouble the Foundation, with the rise of [[Wilder|Mr. Wilder]] who attacked their base in [[Tower of Nostradamus]]. {{Source|The Tower of Nostradamus}}

When the [[Blood Spiral]] revealed itself to the world, the Foundation called an emergency council meeting to respond how to deal with this extremely dangerous new threat. {{Source|Den vs Harrison}} Allied with the [[Casterwill family]], the Foundation sent Dante Vale's team to rescue [[Focauld Casterwill]] from [[the Cloisters]] and to activate the [[Blue Star]] to call the Casterwills out of hiding. {{Source|The Casterwill Connection}} {{Source|The Titan in the Temple of Sun}}

On the longest night of the year, the Huntik Foundation members travelled on [[Scramjets]] to the [[Spiral Mark]] to launch an assault on the [[Blood Spiral Base]]. {{Source|Lok and the Betrayer}} Eventually, after a gruelling final battle, the Huntik Foundation succeeded in defeating the Blood Spiral once and for all. {{source|Dante's Return}}

Three months after the defeat of [[the Betrayer]], Dante Vale officially joined the Huntik Council with [[Lok Lambert]] becoming the new leader of the Foundation's number one team. {{Source|Dante's Return}}

